 "notes": "Stretch 2. Start: p.108 row below the rule (y~430) '1. Re en temt āq er nemmat t'eṭ àn Àusàr Ani àu'; the two rows above (seχem ... unun Àusàr) not read. No footnotes on pp.108-109. Line numerals (Chapter L): '1.' before Re (p.108 title row); '2.' before erṭāt (p.108 row 3 of stretch); '3.' at mid-row before the untransliterated sign preceding 'ent' (p.108 'ḥer ment hru pfi 3. ...' row); '4.' inside user - s (after S29) at start of p.108 row 'user - s ṭepi ...'; '5.' inside θet (after the tether group) on p.108 last row; '6.' inside aśemu (after the owl) on p.109 row 2. Chapter XCIII: '1.' before Re of the title (p.109, below the rule); '2.' inside nui (after G43) on the first row under the 'PLATE XVII.' heading; '3.' at the start of the last row (before useru). Overlines (rubric): p.108 title - one line over Re, en, temt, āq, er (ends before nemmat) and a second over t'eṭ àn; p.109 XCIII title - one line over Re ... t'a - tu (ends after t'a-tu, se not covered) and a second over er àbtet em (Neter-χert not covered); next row: overline over t'eṭ àn. 'en' in the p.108 title: N35 printed in square brackets (restoration); 'à' at the end of seut'a - ten - à printed in brackets [ | ]; in ennuṭ (p.109) the final group (elongated sign over D54) printed in brackets. p.108 row 4: a sign immediately after numeral 3. has no transliteration or English (recorded as budge '—'). Budge prints 'hru' (without dot) twice on p.108 and 't'eṭ' (dotted) on both pages. 'PLATE XVII.' heading on p.109 between the 'Saith Osiris Ani: Hail phallus' row and 'nui ...'; words below it given plate XVII. English '[I],' on p.109 row 3 has no hieroglyph of its own (assigned to Àusàr's gloss). Stretch ends at 'àr àn' / 'So then' at the foot of p.109."
